title: "Privacy-Preserving Data Pipelines"

message: >
  If you use this software or its components in your research,
  please cite it using the metadata provided below.

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Sani
    given-names: Mukhtar

repository-code: https://github.com/sydgep/privacy-preserving-data-pipelines

license: Apache-2.0

abstract: >
  A modular and reproducible framework for developing
  privacy-preserving data pipelines, with a focus on synthetic
  data generation and multidimensional evaluation.
  The framework provides reusable Docker-containerized
  components for data ingestion, preprocessing,
  de-identification, synthetic data generation,
  statistical fidelity assessment, machine learning
  utility evaluation, and privacy risk assessment.
  Components can be executed independently or combined
  into end-to-end workflows using Prefect orchestration.
  The framework supports reproducible research and
  facilitates the development and evaluation of
  privacy-preserving healthcare datasets.

keywords:
  - privacy-preserving data
  - synthetic data generation
  - healthcare
  - statistical fidelity
  - machine learning utility
  - privacy evaluation
  - Docker
  - Prefect
  - workflow orchestration
  - reproducibility

